  another agent (the `parity` -> `stdout_parity` column rename). Committing the
  working-tree file would publish that agent's uncommitted work under this
  commit, so it is held here instead.

  UPDATE — the earlier "cannot be isolated" finding is now STALE. Against the
  old origin/main the rebased hunks died at runtime with "CSV missing required
  column parity". Against current HEAD they apply cleanly (hunk 2 at offset -21)
  and run correctly: verified on both the negative and positive brackets, and
  by the 26-assertion suite in
  compat-envelope/tests/test_render_scorecard_empty_denominator.sh.
  So this CAN now land independently. It is still not committed here only
  because the file's index entry belongs to another agent: whoever lands it
  should `git apply` this patch to HEAD's render-scorecard.rs, not to the
  working-tree copy.

WHAT IT FIXES:
  An EMPTY DENOMINATOR rendered as a confident `TOTAL 0` at exit 0 —
  indistinguishable from "we measured, and nothing passed". Reproduced live on
  two real runs in the committed scorecard.csv, one of which had 24 PASSING
  ptrace cells (in `strict`) and still published 0 under the default `verify`
  denominator. Now refused with exit 3, carrying rows-considered, ptrace-row
  count, and the modes that would actually yield a denominator.

